/-! # Equal-spin D = 5: certificate-level completeness of the reduced system (ATLAS-VI-02/02, D)

For arbitrary radial data `ESData R B D A H W Φ Ψ` (C^∞ on an open set of radii `R`,
`B, D, A, H ≠ 0` there) the Einstein–Maxwell certificate of the candidate's own fields
`esMetric`, `esInverse`, `esFaraday = d(esPotential)` on `esDomain R` holds **iff** the seven
reduced radial equations hold on `R` — given only the explicit signature assumption
`A > 0, H > 0, B D > 0` (used for the `lorentz` field and nothing else). Both directions are
proved; nothing about the field equations is assumed. -/

